# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and on checkout, so
# generated files re-derived on Linux match what was committed from Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except the vendored upstream tests, which are never normalised, never
# converted, and never touched. Their SHA-256 is the evidence that this port
# runs the original suite unmodified, and a line-ending conversion on checkout
# would change those hashes and invalidate the claim.
tests/original/** -text

# Also excluded from GitHub's language statistics, because it is not this
# project's code. tests/original/test_price_parsing.py is 75 KB of vendored
# upstream Python -- 58% of all the Python here -- and counting it made a
# Python-to-Rust port report itself as majority Python, which is precisely
# backwards.
#
# `linguist-vendored` is the marker Linguist provides for third-party code
# carried in-tree, which this is exactly. Our own Python under tools/ stays
# counted: it is real work, it is how the port is verified against the
# original, and hiding it to flatter the bar would misrepresent the repository
# in the other direction.
tests/original/** linguist-vendored
